# Every text file is committed and checked out with LF line endings,
# whatever the platform. Go, YAML, JSON and shell scripts all break or
# churn under CRLF (a shell script with CRLF does not run on ubuntu CI).
* text=auto eol=lf

*.go text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures: only the small synthetic grids and tiles that
# internal/ground's tests generate; real geoid grids and DEM tiles are
# never committed (deploy/fetch-ground.sh fetches them).
*.pgm binary
*.dat binary
